@jamolpe88/dsh-desktop-windowstatus-saving README · dsh-desktop-windowstatus-saving：Zero configuration. Windows only. One Host plugin, no extra process, no network.

**Español** → [README.es.md](README.es.md)

*Without the plugin the window comes back at 1280 × 820 in the default position. With the plugin it comes back at 1943 × 1323 on the same display, and the first painted frame is already final.*

@jamolpe88/dsh-desktop-windowstatus-saving README · Requirements：- **DSH Desktop** `>= 0.2.1-rc.3`, profile `desktop` (tested on `0.2.1-rc.3`, Windows 11).
- Windows 10 or 11. macOS and Linux are not supported.
- Node 22+ (DSH ships its own runtime).

@jamolpe88/dsh-desktop-windowstatus-saving README · State file：`%USERPROFILE%\.dsh\window-bounds.json`, or `$DSH_HOME/window-bounds.json` when `DSH_HOME` is set:

```json
{
  "version": 1,
  "bounds": { "x": -2280, "y": 43, "width": 1943, "height": 1323 },
  "maximized": false,
